/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  liquidDensity04_NaOHpoint -- D3b of the liquid-density pilot (C378).
  The case's OWN measured density of its caustic (constant/experiments/
  NaOH20_303K.dat, 1213.8 kg/m3 at 303.15 K, w[NaOH] 0.20), marked as the
  method of {NaOH, water} and replacing the solution record's law.  1 kg/s of
  the caustic passes the CSTR (V_R 1 m3).  By hand, from the point alone:
      Q   = 1 / 1213.8      = 8.2386e-4 m3/s
      tau = 1 x 1213.8 / 1  = 1213.8 s
  The run prints the law's value beside the point (1212.70, -0.09 %, inside
  the record's stated 2.41 kg/m3).  Move the feed to 333.15 K and the run
  REFUSES: the point stands only in its box; a check-only variant
  (`use check;`) prints "not at its conditions" and prices by the law.
  ONCE THROUGH, NO PUMP: the plan's recycle (a mixer) and a pump both need
  the caustic's liquid heat capacity, which NaOH's record does not carry --
  a gap outside this pilot, reported with it.
  Theory Guide: sec:liquid-density-measured.  Gate: check_density_pilot.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
units
(
    {
        name        R1;
        type        cstr;
        in          feed;
        outputs     ( product );
        operation   { V_R 1; }
        reactions   ( absentSucrose );
    }
);
